<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">Every reading belongs to an asset. <span>Bound to its tag, its unit, and its time zone, so a number never loses what it measured.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-runs">
      <li><h3>Pulled in on a schedule</h3><p>From SCADA, production accounting, IIoT sensors, or any external system. Imports and hand entry cover the rest.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Stored with its context</h3><p>Asset, sensor tag, unit of measure, time zone, and timestamp on every reading.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Corrected without erasing</h3><p>Mark a reading estimated or invalid, or override it. The original value stays on the record.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Open to your tools</h3><p>Readings, flags, and expected ranges in reports, on dashboards, and through the REST API.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">One bad month, caught. <span>The primary generator logged about 300 mcf of fuel a month. In August the record said 9.66.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="top-cards">
      <li class="top-card top-card--wide">
        <div class="top-card-panel">
          <figure class="range-chart">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 120" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <line class="range-base" x1="10" y1="110" x2="290" y2="110"/>
              <rect class="range-band" x="140" y="13.6" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/>
              <line class="range-expected" x1="136" y1="20.6" x2="164" y2="20.6"/>
              <polyline class="range-line" points="30,21.8 90,19.4 150,107.2 210,21.8 270,19.4"/>
              <circle class="range-point" cx="30" cy="21.8" r="3.5"/>
              <circle class="range-point" cx="90" cy="19.4" r="3.5"/>
              <circle class="range-point" cx="210" cy="21.8" r="3.5"/>
              <circle class="range-point" cx="270" cy="19.4" r="3.5"/>
              <circle class="range-flag" cx="150" cy="107.2" r="6"/>
              <text class="range-note" x="150" y="6" text-anchor="middle">Expected range</text>
              <text class="range-note range-note--flag" x="160" y="104">9.66, flagged</text>
            </svg>
            <div class="range-months" aria-hidden="true"><span>Jun</span><span>Jul</span><span>Aug</span><span>Sep</span><span>Oct</span></div>
            <figcaption><span>Fuel use, mcf a month: 299.86, 308.05, <b>9.66</b>, 299.86, 308.05</span><span>August range <b>280.09–327.82</b>, expected <b>303.96</b></span></figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <h3>Checked against its neighbors</h3>
        <p>Each new reading is compared with the readings around it. August fell outside the normal range and was flagged.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="top-card top-card--fill">
        <p class="top-card-cite">Window 7, threshold 3</p>
        <p>The settings on this check. Pick the reading, the date range, and how sensitive each check runs.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="top-card">
        <h3>The flag sits on the asset</h3>
        <p>Not in a separate alarm list. The next step is a work order in the same system.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="top-card">
        <h3>The original stays</h3>
        <p>Confirm it, mark it invalid, or override it. The 9.66 stays in the history either way.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

