<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2>What engineers ask about telemetry.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Which systems can feed it?</summary>
        <div><p>SCADA, production accounting, IIoT sensors, spreadsheets, or any external system, by scheduled pull or import. Readings can also be entered by hand.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does the anomaly check actually do?</summary>
        <div><p>It is univariate: each new reading is compared with its recent neighbors to calculate an expected value with an upper and lower limit. Anything outside is flagged. You set the window and the threshold.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does a flagged reading get deleted?</summary>
        <div><p>No. Mark it estimated or invalid, or override it. The original value stays on the record.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can our analysts pull the data?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. Readings, flags, and expected ranges are available in reports, on dashboards, and through the REST API.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

